    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4110" root="تمر" body-key="t">
    
      4 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اتمر</span></b>  <i>He possessed many,</i> or <i>a large quantity
of,</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَمْر</span> [or <i>dried dates</i>]. (S, M, K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اتمرت</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">النَّخْلَةُ</span>, (T, M, A, K,) and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تمّرت</span></b> , (M, K,) <i>The
palm-tree bore</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَمْر</span> [or <i>dry dates</i>]: (M, K:) or
<i>had ripe dates upon it.</i> (K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اتمر الرُّطَبُ</span>;
(T, K;) and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تمّر</span></b> , inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَتْمِيرٌ</span>; (K;) <i>The ripe
dates became in the state in which they are termed</i>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَمْر</span>. (K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  See also 1.

